# Time Machine — a drag-to-sort todo list (4 items, immediate pan) where every
# reorder pushes a snapshot into a history (jotai atoms); pulling the screen down
# opens the "time machine" (Skia star-field shader background, cards stacked in
# a horizontal snapping list), swiping picks an older snapshot and pulling up
# travels back to it.
# What this test covers: reordering items (down past two rows, back up one),
# a small drag released in place, pulling down to open the time machine, a pull
# released below the threshold (springs back), swiping through history cards
# and past the end, pulling up to close/travel, re-opening, and a fast flick
# open/close.
# NOTE: the history list reads event.contentOffset.y on a horizontal ScrollView,
# so the stacked-card transforms and the selected snapshot never change and
# swiping leaves the cards off-screen after closing — see report.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/time-machine"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 45000
# Warm-up touch on the status bar: the first touch of a test can be lost while
# the XCTest runner attaches.
press 330 20
wait 500
wait "text" "Buy groceries" 10000
wait 1000
# Reorder: first row down two rows, then the second row up one.
gesture pan 220 331 0 220 800
wait 1200
gesture pan 220 401 0 -70 600
wait 1200
gesture pan 220 471 0 10 300
wait 1000
# Pull down less than the threshold (springs closed), then fully open.
gesture pan 200 620 0 60 600
wait 1200
gesture pan 200 620 0 200 500
wait 2000
# Swipe through the history cards and beyond the last one.
gesture pan 300 440 -220 0 500
wait 1200
gesture pan 300 440 -220 0 500
wait 1200
gesture pan 100 440 200 0 500
wait 1200
# Pull up: close the time machine (travel to the selected snapshot).
gesture pan 200 700 0 -250 400
wait 2500
# Open again and close with a fast flick.
gesture pan 200 500 0 200 150
wait 1500
gesture pan 200 700 0 -250 150
wait 2500
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
